 about the cosmos. Our expert astronomer, Dr. Celestial, will guide you through the night sky, revealing hidden celestial wonders and the mysteries of the universe.\n\n### Main Telescope Experience\n\nAs the night unfolds, the main telescope at our observatory transforms into a captivating instrument. The covered dome shelters it from the elements, providing a safe and comfortable environment for detailed observations. This is where you can witness the mesmerizing process of images of stars, galaxies, and other celestial phenomena being captured by the telescope\u2019s lenses.\n\n### Weather Conditions and Session Location\n\nDespite the beautiful view outside, the current weather conditions require us to move indoors. This indoor setting offers a more controlled environment for observing under more favorable conditions, such as clear skies and a comfortable seating area. The event will conclude at 21:00, ensuring you have plenty of time to fully engage with the night sky and learn about the wonders of astronomy.\n\n### Closure and Reflection\n\nAs the night draws to a close, the welcoming group of students and astronomy enthusiasts will gather to reflect on the evening's experiences. Dr. Celestial will lead a discussion, highlighting the incredible discoveries and scientific advancements made through astronomical observation. This session is open to everyone and provides a wonderful opportunity to deepen your knowledge and appreciation of the cosmos.", "cap": false, "prompt_ids": [151644, 8948, 198, 2610, 525, 1207, 16948, 11, 3465, 553, 54364, 14817, 13, 1446, 525, 264, 10950, 17847, 13, 151645, 198, 151644, 872, 198, 7985, 264, 43388, 20181, 42536, 315, 911, 220, 16, 23, 15, 311, 220, 17, 17, 15, 4244, 911, 458, 9282, 5269, 1787, 1899, 13, 5443, 1172, 279, 2701, 584, 3255, 369, 14175, 3565, 13, 29734, 1817, 315, 1181, 3040, 22870, 6896, 11, 323, 912, 5390, 16148, 2163, 1105, 13, 3155, 537, 912, 264, 855, 1564, 911, 1493, 11221, 382, 12676, 3255, 510, 785, 10565, 